# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the grep ASAN test build.
#
# The in-tree regex engine (usr.lib/regex) leaks the regex_charclass
# allocation for a bracket/character-class node: node_free() does not release
# node->charclass.  It is a bounded, compile-time leak (one allocation per
# character class in a pattern, NOT per input line) and is a pre-existing
# defect in the shared engine, out of scope for the grep work.  Suppress it so
# the leak check still verifies that grep's OWN allocations (patterns, context
# ring, line buffer, file vector, include/exclude lists) are all freed.
leak:parse_concat
leak:charclass_new
leak:engine_safe.c
